      "id": "https://knightcenter.utexas.edu/?p=100827",
      "title": "AI, trust and the future of journalism took center stage at ISOJ 2026",
      "link": "https://knightcenter.utexas.edu/ai-trust-and-the-future-of-journalism-took-center-stage-at-isoj-2026/",
      "published": "Wed, 23 Sep 2026 17:46:20 +0000",
      "summary_raw": "<p>The future of journalism rests on technology and the human relationships that connect news organizations with their audiences. That was the central theme of the 27th International Symposium on Journalism (ISOJ), held Sept. 17-18 at the University of Texas at Austin and broadcast online. The annual conference organized by the Knight Center for Journalism in [&#8230;]</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://knightcenter.utexas.edu/ai-trust-and-the-future-of-journalism-took-center-stage-at-isoj-2026/\">AI, trust and the future of journalism took center stage at ISOJ 2026</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://knightcenter.utexas.edu\">Knight Center for Journalism in the Americas</a>.</p>",
      "source": "Knight Center / LatAm Journalism Review"
    },
    {
      "id": "https://knightcenter.utexas.edu/?p=100814",
      "title": "Mexican journalist Carmen Aristegui on putting people at the center of journalism",
      "link": "https://knightcenter.utexas.edu/mexican-journalist-carmen-aristegui-on-putting-people-at-the-center-of-journalism/",
      "published": "Wed, 23 Sep 2026 17:22:17 +0000",
      "summary_raw": "<p>Talking about the future of journalism makes little sense without addressing the converging crises of the rise of authoritarianism, the expansion of AI and climate change — forces that are driving a civilizational shift for humanity. That was how Mexican journalism pioneer Carmen Aristegui opened her keynote address at the 19th Ibero-American Journalism Colloquium(opens in [&#8230;]</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://knightcenter.utexas.edu/mexican-journalist-carmen-aristegui-on-putting-people-at-the-center-of-journalism/\">Mexican journalist Carmen Aristegui on putting people at the center of journalism</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://knightcenter.utexas.edu\">Knight Center for Journalism in the Americas</a>.</p>",
      "source": "Knight Center / LatAm Journalism Review"
    },
    {
      "id": "https://knightcenter.utexas.edu/?p=100804",
      "title": "ISOJ 2026 Day 2: Publishers are facing a new middleman as AI changes the business",
      "link": "https://knightcenter.utexas.edu/isoj-2026-day-2-publishers-are-facing-a-new-middleman-as-ai-changes-the-business/",
      "published": "Wed, 23 Sep 2026 16:52:34 +0000",
      "summary_raw": "<p>The news business is confronting an existential paradox: AI technology can make journalism faster and cheaper but it also threatens the audience and revenue that sustain it. That tension dominated the second day of the 27th International Symposium on Journalism, where news executives and journalists on Friday debated AI-powered workflows, new products, falling web traffic and [&#8230;]</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://knightcenter.utexas.edu/isoj-2026-day-2-publishers-are-facing-a-new-middleman-as-ai-changes-the-business/\">ISOJ 2026 Day 2: Publishers are facing a new middleman as AI changes the business</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://knightcenter.utexas.edu\">Knight Center for Journalism in the Americas</a>.</p>",
      "source": "Knight Center / LatAm Journalism Review"
    },
    {
      "id": "https://knightcenter.utexas.edu/?p=100794",
      "title": "Nonprofit news is betting on unorthodox ways to grow",
      "link": "https://knightcenter.utexas.edu/nonprofit-news-is-betting-on-unorthodox-ways-to-grow/",
      "published": "Wed, 23 Sep 2026 16:39:08 +0000",
      "summary_raw": "<p>Local public and nonprofit news organizations are getting creative about surviving an industry that keeps getting smaller. They’re buying or launching smaller publications, joining forces with community groups, and looking for ways to grow. At Chicago Public Media, the bet is that public media needs to reclaim its role as a public square—much as it [&#8230;]</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://knightcenter.utexas.edu/nonprofit-news-is-betting-on-unorthodox-ways-to-grow/\">Nonprofit news is betting on unorthodox ways to grow</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://knightcenter.utexas.edu\">Knight Center for Journalism in the Americas</a>.</p>",
      "source": "Knight Center / LatAm Journalism Review"
    },
    {
      "id": "https://knightcenter.utexas.edu/?p=100765",
      "title": "Ibero-American journalists respond to AI and democratic crises with collaboration and innovation",
      "link": "https://knightcenter.utexas.edu/ibero-american-journalists-respond-to-ai-and-democratic-crises-with-collaboration-and-innovation/",
      "published": "Tue, 22 Sep 2026 17:49:43 +0000",
      "summary_raw": "<p>Ibero-American journalists are betting on collaboration, creativity and independent journalism to confront the existential challenges facing the industry and humanity today — from democratic crises around the world to the rise of artificial intelligence. Those were some of the central themes of the 19th Ibero-American Journalism Colloquium, held Sept. 19 at the University of Texas [&#8230;]</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://knightcenter.utexas.edu/ibero-american-journalists-respond-to-ai-and-democratic-crises-with-collaboration-and-innovation/\">Ibero-American journalists respond to AI and democratic crises with collaboration and innovation</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://knightcenter.utexas.edu\">Knight Center for Journalism in the Americas</a>.</p>",
      "source": "Knight Center / LatAm Journalism Review"
    }
